{
  "_note": [
    "Raid planner: structures and their maximum HP. Hand-collected, not extracted.",
    "maxHp = HP of the fully built, healthy structure. null = not measured yet.",
    "Building blocks (walls, foundations, floors...) are entities, not Rust items, so",
    "their keys are synthetic, of the form <block>.<grade> (wall.stone, foundation.wood,",
    "floor.metal, ...). Deployables (doors, high externals, barricades...) use their real",
    "Rust item shortname.",
    "category: free-form tag for the future hierarchical menu (block:twig / block:wood /",
    "block:stone / block:metal / block:armored / door / gate / external / deployable).",
    "The menu tree itself will be decided later from these tags.",
    "Fill _patch with the game version the numbers were measured on.",
    "sides: set to true on structures whose soft/hard faces take different damage from",
    "side-sensitive weapons (walls, foundations...). The side-specific damage values live",
    "in raid-damage.json as <key>.soft / <key>.hard entries; this file never has per-side",
    "entries, maxHp is the same on both faces.",
    "We consider walls, wall frames, door frames, roofs, foundations and floors as walls",
    "this keeps the document shorter as they all share the same HP and side properties.",
    "Similarly, we consider both ramps and stairs as stairs.",
    "we ignore double variants of doors - they have identical properties to single doors in terms of raiding"
  ],
